  "text": ".color[\n.WriteHeader(1) {\n\\color{blue} \\textbf{Problem:}\nEach of the 12 dots in this figure is to be colored yellow, green, or purple. No two dots connected by a segment (with no other dots between) may be the same color. How many ways are there to color the dots of this figure?\n\n.WriteHeader(2) {\n\\color{red} \\textbf{Solution:}\nWe will solve this problem using the principle of inclusion-exclusion.\n\n.WriteHeader(3) {\n\\color{blue} \\textbf{Step 1:}\nLet's count the total number of ways to color the dots without any restrictions. Since there are 3 colors and 12 dots, the total number of ways is $3^{12}$.\n\n.WriteHeader(4) {\n\\color{red} \\textbf{Step 2:}\nNow, we need to subtract the number of ways where at least one pair of connected dots are the same color. There are 9 pairs of connected dots, and for each pair, there are $2^12$ ways to color them the same color (since we have 2 choices for the color and 12 dots).\n\n.WriteHeader(5) {\n\\color{blue} \\textbf{Step 3:}\nHowever, we have subtracted too much because we have subtracted the cases where two pairs of connected dots are the same color twice. There are $\\binom{9}{2}$ ways to choose two pairs, and for each pair, there are $1^12$ ways to color them the same color.\n\n.WriteHeader(6) {\n\\color{red} \\textbf{Step 4:}\nFinally, we need to add back the cases where three pairs of connected dots are the same color. There are $\\binom{9}{3}$ ways to choose three pairs, and for each pair, there are $0^12$ ways to color them the same color.\n\n.WriteHeader(7) {\n\\color{blue} \\textbf{Step 5:}\nPutting it all together, the number of ways to color the dots is:\n\\[3^{12} - \\binom{9}{1}2^{12} + \\binom{9}{2}1^{12} - \\binom{9}{3}0^{12}.\\]\n\n.WriteHeader(8) {\n\\color{red} \\textbf{Step 6:}\nCalculating the values, we get:\n\\[3^{12} - 9 \\cdot 2^{12} + 36 \\cdot 1^{12} - 84 \\cdot 0^{12} = 531441 - 9 \\cdot 4096 + 36 \\cdot 1 - 84 \\cdot 0 = 531441 - 36864 + 36 = 494577.\\]\n\n.WriteHeader(9) {\n\\color{blue} \\textbf{Answer:}\nTherefore, the number of ways to color the dots of the figure is $\\boxed{494577}$.",
